570 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText ( The process begins when a client arrives at the store. The store receptionist greets the customer and asks if they are already registered in the system. If the customer is registered, the process continues directly to the order-taking phase. If the customer is not registered, they are asked if they would like to create a profile. For those who agree, their information, including name, address, and VAT number, is collected and entered into the system. If the customer does not wish to register, the process skips this step and proceeds to order-taking.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
571 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText ( After registration \(or skipping it\), the receptionist asks the customer for their order and answers any additional questions. The payment method is then chosen, either cash or card, followed by verifying the fiscal \(VAT\) number twice to ensure accuracy. Once all details are confirmed, the order is finalized and marked as fulfilled. This completes the in-person order registration process.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
