914 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (In the AS-IS scenario for the "Order-to-Cash" process, the average process time was 198.85 seconds \(approximately 3.31 minutes\). This includes all tasks, from the customer placing the call to the completion of the order. The phone operator's utilization was 30.21%, indicating that they are handling the workload efficiently without being overburdened.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
915 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The most time-intensive tasks in the process were Order Fulfillment, taking an average of 178.92 seconds \(around 2.98 minutes\), and Registering Information in the Database, which averaged 103.52 seconds \(approximately 1.72 minutes\). These tasks represent significant portions of the overall process time.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
916 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Despite these time-intensive steps, the simulation shows minimal or no waiting times for tasks, suggesting that the current setup with one phone operator effectively meets the demand. However, opportunities exist to optimize tasks like database entry and fulfillment to further reduce the overall process time.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
