<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (In Scenario 2, where the number of website operators was reduced to one, the process experienced significant delays and inefficiencies. The average processing time increased to 375.68 seconds \(6 minutes and 16 seconds\), significantly higher than in scenarios with more operators. Total waiting time also escalated to 22,987.39 seconds \(6 hours, 23 minutes, and 7 seconds\), indicating severe bottlenecks.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
1105 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Key observations include:)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
1106 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 6367 0 R
/ActualText ("Enter customer phone number into the orders IS": Average task time was 100.13 seconds \(1 minute and 40 seconds\), with a total waiting time of 7,120.01 seconds \(1 hour, 58 minutes, and 40 seconds\).)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1107 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 6368 0 R
/ActualText ("Verify if it is a customer with a different number": Average time of 67.60 seconds \(1 minute and 7 seconds\) and total waiting time of 2,974.80 seconds \(49 minutes and 34 seconds\).)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1108 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 6369 0 R
/ActualText ("Transfer the call to the right store": Average waiting time increased to 48.11 seconds \(48 seconds\), with a total waiting time of 866.08 seconds \(14 minutes and 26 seconds\).)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1109 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 6370 0 R
/ActualText (Order Fulfillment: Waiting time alone averaged 219.16 seconds \(3 minutes and 39 seconds\), indicating delays throughout the end-to-end process.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1110 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (While reducing to one operator cuts costs, the sharp rise in waiting times and inefficiencies makes this scenario unsustainable. These delays would result in poor customer experiences, unfulfilled demand, and potential financial losses, outweighing the cost-saving benefits. Maintaining a minimum of two operators is crucial for balancing efficiency and cost-effectiveness.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
