1215 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Orders registered by the website)
/E (Orders registered by the website)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
1216 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The company registered a total of 5250 orders. Out of these, 25.5 percent were placed through the website, amounting to 1340 orders. On average, this translates to 45 orders per day registered on the website over a 30-day period.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
1217 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The website operates for 5 hours per day, which is equivalent to 18,000 seconds \(5 hours x 60 minutes x 60 seconds\). To calculate the mean arrival rate \(lambda\), we divide the total daily orders by the total number of seconds:)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
1218 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Mean arrival rate \(lambda\) = 45 orders / 18,000 s = 0.0025 orders per second)
/E (Mean arrival rate \(lambda\) = 45 orders / 18,000 s = 0.0025 orders per second)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1219 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The mean inter-arrival time, representing the average time between two consecutive orders, is the reciprocal of lambda:)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1220 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Mean inter-arrival time = 1 / 0.0025 = 400 seconds)
/E (Mean inter-arrival time = 1 / 0.0025 = 400 seconds)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1221 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (This means, on average, a website order is placed every 400 seconds \(approximately 6.67 minutes\).)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
