/ActualText (The total process time, however, rose significantly from 8,686.56 seconds \(144.78 minutes\) in the AS-IS scenario to 13,155.54 seconds \(219.26 minutes\), reflecting the increased workload.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1428 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The employee's utilization rate also increased from 48.7% in the AS-IS scenario to 77.26%, highlighting a much heavier workload. While the system still operates without delays or waiting times, this high utilization indicates the employee is nearing capacity.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1429 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (If demand continues to rise or unexpected issues occur, this setup may lead to delays or inefficiencies. Further adjustments, such as adding more staff or streamlining tasks, may be needed to sustain higher workloads effectively.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
