/Pg 62 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
2799 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The reduction in errors also alleviated the workload for resources. The Packager utilization decreased from 83.88% in the As-Is scenario to 72.45%, and the Courier utilization dropped from 84.67% to 65.57%, providing additional flexibility during peak periods. The Manager utilization remained stable at 80.21%, reflecting consistent performance.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 62 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
2800 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText <>
/Alt ()
/Pg 62 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
2801 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText ( This scenario demonstrates the importance of quality control. Reducing the error rate led to shorter average process times, better resource balance, and fewer disruptions, resulting in a more efficient overall process.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 62 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
