2833 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Orders Registered at the Store have been consistently efficient based on prior simulations and analysis. Hence we concluded that the Order Registered at the Store process does not require any changes in the To-Be model. After testing various scenarios in previous simulations, as detailed in the report, we observed that this process consistently performed efficiently across all situations. The simulations demonstrated that the process is already optimized in terms of task execution, resource utilization, and customer satisfaction.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 67 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
2834 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (In every scenario tested, the process showed no significant bottlenecks, delays, or errors that would necessitate further improvements. Additionally, the resource allocation was balanced, and the workflow structure supported seamless and accurate order registration. Based on these findings, we determined that the current state of the Order Registered at the Store process is well-suited to meet operational needs and does not require further adjustments in the To-Be model.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 67 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
2835 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (This allows us to focus on improving other areas of the order process, such as phone or online order registration, where optimization opportunities are more apparent.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 67 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
