3341 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Limitations)
/E (Limitations)
/Alt ()
/Pg 77 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
3342 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (While the redesigned processes and analyses provide a clear pathway to improving efficiency and reducing costs, several limitations should be considered when interpreting the results and implementing the proposed changes.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 77 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
3343 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (1. Data Limitations)
/E (1. Data Limitations)
/Alt ()
/Pg 77 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
3344 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The analysis relies on simulated scenarios and assumptions based on average operational data, such as employee salaries, task durations, and customer arrival rates. Any inaccuracies or variations in these inputs could affect the outcomes of the analysis. Additionally, some data, such as real-world system integration costs or unanticipated workflow interruptions, were not fully available and required estimation.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 77 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
3345 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (2. Assumptions in Costing and Workforce)
/E (2. Assumptions in Costing and Workforce)
/Alt ()
/Pg 77 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
3346 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The cost estimates for one-time and recurring expenses, such as Toast POS, mobile plans, and training, were based on current market rates. Actual costs may vary depending on vendor negotiations, regional factors, or future price changes. Similarly, workforce changes, such as the removal of the manager role and reallocation of tasks, were based on theoretical models and may not fully capture the complexities of real-world organizational adjustments.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 77 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
3347 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (3. System and Technology Limitations)
/E (3. System and Technology Limitations)
/Alt ()
/Pg 77 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
3348 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Implementing new systems like Toast POS and delivery routing APIs may present unforeseen technical challenges, including integration issues with existing infrastructure or downtime during deployment. Additionally, training employees to effectively use these tools may require more time and resources than initially anticipated.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 77 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
3349 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (4. External Market Factors)
/E (4. External Market Factors)
/Alt ()
/Pg 77 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
3350 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (External influences, such as market competition, inflation, or technological advancements, could affect the long-term viability of the proposed solutions. Ongoing monitoring and adaptability will be necessary to address these factors.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 77 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
3351 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (By acknowledging these limitations, the report emphasizes the need for a flexible and iterative approach to process improvements, ensuring that the proposed models remain relevant and effective under evolving conditions.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 77 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
3352 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 436 0 R
/Pg 77 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
3353 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 436 0 R
/Pg 77 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
3354 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Conclusion)
/E (Conclusion)
/Alt ()
/Pg 78 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
3355 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (To remain competitive in the rapidly evolving food delivery market, Home Burger must address inefficiencies within its Order-to-Cash \(O2C\) process. The analysis conducted in this study has identified critical areas for improvement, including resource imbalances, manual task dependencies, and process bottlenecks. These issues not only affect operational efficiency but also have a direct impact on customer satisfaction and cost management.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 78 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
3356 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Key findings indicate that high resource utilization in certain roles, such as kitchen staff and managers, creates bottlenecks that delay order processing and delivery. Manual workflows, including repetitive data entry and order verification tasks, further worsen inefficiencies, leading to avoidable errors and increased processing times. )
/Alt ()
/Pg 78 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
3357 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (To address these challenges, the proposed recommendations include automating redundant tasks, balancing workloads through resource reallocation, and refining task responsibilities across roles. Simulations of proposed changes demonstrate significant reductions in process time, resource strain, and error rates. These adjustments enable smoother workflow transitions, improved scalability, and enhanced customer experiences.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 78 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
3358 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (By implementing these changes, Home Burger will improve its operational performance, reduce costs, and increase its capacity to manage growing demand effectively. These improvements will strengthen its competitive position, ensure long-term sustainability, and enhance its reputation as a leader in the food delivery industry.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 78 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
